; Divide: 25 / 5, with loops
; The same as dividing ball by ball, but the hand repeats START until
; something happens. Change the two SET lines to divide other numbers
; (the quotient must be under 7). Reading the answer: cycles = 7 - MQ;
; if A is 0 the quotient is the cycles and the remainder 0, otherwise
; the quotient is cycles - 1 and the remainder M - A.

R               ; reset: COUNT on
SET A 25        ; the dividend
X Space X Space ; complement it: A = 103 = 128 - 25
SET M 5         ; the divisor
SET MQ 7        ; the counter
D               ; distributor set to begin a cycle
M               ; MULTIPLY on
UNTIL OVERFLOW  ; cycle after cycle, until A goes over 128
UNTIL CYCLE     ; then on to the end of that cycle
CHECK A 0       ; 0: it went exactly
CHECK MQ 2      ; 7 - 2 = 5 cycles: 25 / 5 = 5
